---
description: Security gate for generated and modified code
alwaysApply: true
---

- For newly generated or modified first-party code, run a lightweight security review before finalizing changes.
- Check input validation, auth/permission flaws, secrets exposure, injection risks, SSRF, path traversal, unsafe file handling, and insecure defaults.
- If findings are returned, fix them before finishing.
- Do not introduce secrets into code, tests, docs, examples, or commits.
- Prefer parameterized queries, strict schema validation, least-privilege auth checks, and safe defaults.
